From: "Pluet, LLC" <358065800+pluetllc@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:47:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] stream: play Blu-ray and DVD disc images read through mpv's
 streams (disc://)

A disc image (.iso) that is not a local file could not play as a disc:
libbluray and libdvdnav open paths only. A media server sends an image
over http(s), and a network share through Pluet's own byte server, so
neither reached the disc code.

libbluray (bd_open_stream) and libdvdread (dvdnav_open_stream2) both take
a block reader. disc://<address> opens the address with stream_create and
hands its sectors to libbluray, then to libdvdnav if it is not a Blu-ray.
The main title plays (or --edition's), the other titles are editions and
the chapters are the title's, exactly as for bd:// and dvd://.

Only random access is needed, no directory listing, so any seekable mpv
stream works. Folders (BDMV, VIDEO_TS) still need a local path.
